  "narrative": "This wave mostly provides negative evidence for the registered less-common-state/stronger-dependency hypothesis, with one important direction reversal. For outcome_012 and outcome_015 the approximate 10% absolute dependency-scale thresholds are about 0.025; outcome_006 is about 0.0175; outcome_001 is about 0.0415. H70 and H71 for feature_007 are far below those clinical sizes and have intervals that include zero, so they are rejected and closed. H72 is the key new result: under the registered negative direction, the signed estimate is -0.0642 with signed interval [-0.1211, -0.0074]. Because the interval is entirely on the wrong side of zero, the raw exposed-minus-comparator contrast is positive by about 0.064 on outcome_006, i.e. feature_007 exposure is associated with weaker rather than stronger dependency for that outcome. This raw magnitude is clinically large relative to outcome_006, but the pre-registered H72 direction is contradicted, so H72 itself must be rejected and closed. Since reversing a direction after seeing discovery data is multiplicity-prone, I do not accept this reversal here. Instead, I register a new positive-direction refinement for the same raw contrast so that a correctly signed analysis can later be run and, if warranted, independently validated. H73 is the same predictor on outcome_001 and shows a similar opposite-direction point estimate, but its signed interval still includes zero; it is not enough to establish the reversal and is rejected/closed as written. H74-H77 for feature_047 are small, wrong-direction, or null-inclusive, so all are rejected and closed. For feature_023, H78 and H79 are not clinically supported in the registered direction and are rejected/closed. H80 and H81 are different: both have signed estimates in the registered negative direction that exceed the approximate 10% thresholds, and their lower bounds are close to zero, but the 95% intervals include zero. Given the multiplicity-heavy screen and the fact that the same predictor drives both borderline signals, I keep them unresolved and deferred rather than closed, but they are not accepted. I do not request validation now because the strongest immediate candidate, H72, is a rejected opposite-direction claim; validating H72 would be signed to the wrong scientific claim. Next, the positive feature_007/outcome_006 refinement should be analyzed with the correct direction, and if it reproduces the clinically sized interval excluding zero, it should be the first validation target. All conclusions remain dataset associations only.",
