  "narrative": "All twelve newly delivered comparisons are valid Welch tests with sufficient cell counts. H266 and H267 complete the feature_057 10-versus-5 dose-response family for outcome_011 and outcome_013. H266 has a positive signed estimate of only +0.0144 but a 95% interval from -0.0236 to +0.0523, crossing zero and below the practical benchmark for outcome_011. H267 has a negative signed estimate of -0.0221 with interval -0.0540 to +0.0098, which is both imprecise and opposite the hypothesized direction. I reject both and close the remaining feature_057 contrast family.\n\nThe most informative new evidence is the set of feature_050-outcome_001 stratified tests H271-H277. These are direction -1 claims, so positive signed estimates mean feature_050=1 is associated with a more negative outcome_001 dependency score than feature_050=0 within the specified stratum. Every stratum estimate is large and positive: feature_061<=59 +0.7677; low feature_018 +0.7677; high feature_018 +0.8071; low feature_016 +0.7543; high feature_016 +0.7840; high feature_053 +0.7663; and low feature_053 +0.7930. Every lower confidence bound is at least +0.7119, which is not merely above the outcome_001 10%-of-absolute-mean benchmark of about +0.0415 but roughly eighteen times larger. I therefore accept H271-H277 as additional dataset-specific stratified replicates of the already accepted feature_050 association. These results do not establish a new predictor, causal effect, biological mechanism, or external generalizability; they show that the enormous association is internally consistent across several nontrivial numeric strata and not attenuated to practical null in any tested stratum.\n\nH278 tests the focused rare-level feature_048 contrast, level_002 versus level_001 for outcome_001. The signed estimate is +0.1594, a potentially meaningful point size, but the 95% interval is -0.0205 to +0.3393 and the exposed cell has only 25 observations. The lower bound is below zero and far below the practical acceptance threshold. I therefore reject H278 as clinically meaningful evidence and close it. I also close the linked/refined opposite-direction claim H149 because the same contrast does not support that claim and remains imprecise. H279 and H280 extend the feature_055 level_004 versus level_003 family to outcome_009 and outcome_010. Both are close to null: +0.0016 and +0.0049, with intervals crossing zero and point estimates below their practical benchmarks. I reject and close them.\n\nNo validation is requested. The accepted stratum results are internal replicates of an already independently validated central association, and the only candidate second signal, H278, is too imprecise to justify an independent test. The final validation allowance is not used because there is no new precise exception or unresolved modification claim meeting the practical-significance standard.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 18 appraise: all due claims resolved. H271-H277 accept and close the feature_050-outcome_001 stratified replication battery across feature_061<=59, feature_018 low/high, feature_016 low/high, and feature_053 low/high; all effects remain near the full-population estimate and far above the outcome_001 10% absolute-mean benchmark. H266/H267 reject and close remaining feature_057 10-versus-5 contrasts. H278 rejects the rare-level feature_048 level_002 versus level_001 signal because its interval is wide, crosses zero, and has lower bound below threshold; H149 is also rejected and closed. H279/H280 reject feature_055 level_004 versus level_003 on outcome_009 and outcome_010. No validation requested: no unresolved precise candidate remains. The evidence-supported in-dataset conclusion remains the very large, internally robust but interpretation-limited feature_050=1 versus 0 association with stronger negative outcome_001; no robust second clinically meaningful association was found."
