  "narrative": "Final scientific report.\n\nNo assessments were due and no new validation result or response deadline was delivered in this synthesis. I therefore do not reassess a validation deadline. I do not use the remaining voluntary validation request because the central association has already been independently validated and the unresolved issues are biological interpretation, causal attribution, and external generalizability, not whether another in-dataset null contrast should be validated. I made three optional closure reassessments, H291 to H293, because they are closed unresolved conditional claims with direct evidence that clearly cannot support practical significance. For outcome_001 with direction plus one, the signed estimates are negative and the upper bounds are well below the approximately plus 0.0415 practical threshold, so each is rejected.\n\nSupported finding. The only scientifically meaningful in-dataset association supported by the accumulated evidence is outcome_001, feature_050 exposed level one versus comparator level zero. H99 discovery R61 gives signed plus 0.784 with 95 percent interval plus 0.765 to plus 0.803. Independent validation R65 gives signed plus 0.793 with independent interval plus 0.763 to plus 0.822. Because direction was registered as minus one, positive signed estimates mean the raw feature_050 one minus feature_050 zero difference is negative. Since more negative CRISPR dependency scores mean stronger dependency, feature_050 equals one is associated with substantially stronger outcome_001 dependency. The raw effect is approximately minus 0.78 to minus 0.79 outcome units. Relative to the approximate outcome_001 ten percent practical scale of about 0.0415 absolute score units, the validated lower bound is nearly twenty times larger. The finding is therefore large, internally reproducible across strata, and not marginal.\n\nSubgroup interpretation. Many accepted claims are stratum-specific feature_050 outcome_001 mean differences across binary, categorical, continuous, median-split, complete-case, quality-control-like, and demographic-like strata. They should be interpreted as repeated evidence for the same dominant feature_050 signal within this dataset, not as many independent biological predictors or independently validated subgroups. The interactions that tested whether other measured variables modify this central association were mostly null or below the practical-significance criterion. The one validated interaction involving feature_014, H260, reversed in validation R216 and is not supported. Thus, the accepted evidence supports a very strong main association, but not a set of robust independent modifiers in the supplied data.\n\nNegative findings. Across the sixteen CRISPR dependency outcomes, the broad and focused predictor screens did not produce another robust association meeting the ten percent practical-significance criterion. Several discovery signals were refuted or weakened by independent validation: outcome_006 with feature_042 R25, outcome_006 with feature_020 R38, outcome_006 with feature_060 R39, outcome_006 with feature_023 R52, outcome_006 with feature_037 R79, outcome_006 with feature_007 R92 and subgroup R106, outcome_005 with feature_007 R105, outcome_010 with feature_050 R78, outcome_006 with feature_009 R119, and the feature_014 interaction on the central association R216. Other nominal discovery estimates, such as feature_055 contrasts for outcome_008 and small negative dependency contrasts for outcome_006 or outcome_001, failed because their lower bounds did not exceed the practical threshold. The final residual scan within the feature_050 equals zero population, H333 to H340, also found no clinically meaningful residual positive association with outcome_001. These are negative findings for scientifically meaningful effects, not proofs of exact nullity or equivalence for very small effects.\n\nUnresolved uncertainty. The primary uncertainty is interpretation. Predictor labels are opaque, so feature_050 may represent a true biological state, clinical or lineage status, copy-number or expression structure, cell-line or sample identity, batch or pipeline artifact, QC or missingness surrogate, or another dataset-specific surrogate. The stratum analyses show that the association is not limited to one arbitrary subgroup, but they cannot establish what feature_050 means or that the association is causal. Conditioning on feature_050 equals zero in residual analyses may also induce selection or collider-like dependence, so those null results do not prove that other predictors have no biological association. Complete-case and quality-control-like strata reduce one concern but do not eliminate artifact risk. Generalizability outside this dataset remains unproven.\n\nMost informative next analysis. The next analysis should be external and confirmatory rather than another broad in-dataset scan. The highest value is to characterize feature_050 using independent metadata or independent replication: test its relation to sample or cell-line identity, plate, batch, library or sequencing metrics, missingness and QC patterns, copy-number or expression structure, clinical metadata, and pipeline variables; adjust the outcome_001 association for these candidate surrogates; and replicate the feature_050 outcome_001 dependency contrast in an independent CRISPR dependency dataset. If further in-dataset follow-up is unavoidable, it should be tightly pre-specified and judged by the practical lower-bound criterion rather than nominal significance alone.\n\nFinal conclusion. In this supplied dataset, the evidence supports one robust, large, independently validated association: feature_050 equals one is associated with markedly stronger outcome_001 CRISPR dependency. The evidence does not support another measured predictor or subgroup modifier with a scientifically meaningful difference in any of the sixteen dependency outcomes. The causal, mechanistic, and external-generalizability status of the central feature_050 association remains unresolved.",
